= Burden of Government

Taking ministries makes every cabinet compromise part of Lewica's record.
Workers, tenants, patients and equality movements expect more than access to
the coalition council. During each six-month window, complete at least **two
distinct goals**:

<ul>
<li>strengthen the public health service;</li>
<li>build public housing or improve tenant security;</li>
<li>expand labour rights or enforcement;</li>
<li>strengthen the social floor and public services;</li>
<li>enact material equality protections.</li>
</ul>

Government Affairs cards and guarded coalition events advance these goals.
Accepting an explicitly marketising or anti-social settlement breaches the
whole window, as conservative policy did in the original Weimar burden.

- @entry_continue

